{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CAL3AnchorStructure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.CAL3AnchorStructure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CAL3Anchor.S_welldefined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CAL3Anchor.S_welldefined","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CAL3AnchorStructure.lean#L81-L90","doc":"**`S` is the single archimedean leak (not derived).** The identity\n`S = c_3^odd / κ_(2,1)(q_0)` merely *defines* `S`; it carries no content until\n`S` is fixed independently. The open keystone is the identification of `S`\nwith a CAL-3-class quantity `g(P_avg^π)` — deliberately not axiomatised (a class\n`S = g P_avg^π` is vacuously satisfiable; the real content is cross-anchor\nrigidity of a single categorical `g`, which is unproved). This lemma records\nonly the trivial well-definedness of the defining ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CAL3Anchor.c3_swing_factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CAL3Anchor.c3_swing_factorization","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CAL3AnchorStructure.lean#L71-L79","doc":"**The cross-anchor swing is isolated in `S`.** For nonzero carriers, the ratio\nof the factorized odd channel at two anchors factors into the pure-q carrier\nratio times the scalar ratio: `(κa·Sa)/(κb·Sb) = (κa/κb)·(Sa/Sb)`. Since `κ`\nis a pure-q function (anchor-rigid to the ppb the anchors differ by), the\nentire c_3 cross-anchor swing lives in `Sa/Sb`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CAL3Anchor.c3odd_bar_odd_of_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CAL3Anchor.c3odd_bar_odd_of_factor","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CAL3AnchorStructure.lean#L61-L69","doc":"**The odd-channel factorization sits in the bar-odd part.** If the `c_3` odd\nchannel is `κ·S` with `κ` bar-odd (`σ κ = −κ`, the carrier) and `S` bar-fixed\n(`σ S = S`, an archimedean constant), then it is bar-odd. The parity is\ninherited from the carrier `κ`, NOT from the archimedean scalar `S` — so\nanchoring `S` cannot change the channel's parity (consistent with the\nstanding reading KC6/KC10: parity gates test the odd part). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CAL3Anchor.kappa21_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CAL3Anchor.kappa21_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CAL3AnchorStructure.lean#L49-L59","doc":"**The carrier is nonzero away from `q ∈ {0, 1, −1}`.** Hence\n`S := c_3^odd / κ_(2,1)(q_0)` is well-defined at the substrate anchor\n(`q_0 ≈ 1.11 ∉ {0,1,−1}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CAL3Anchor.kappa21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CAL3Anchor.kappa21","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CAL3AnchorStructure.lean#L44-L47","doc":"The derived bar-odd fibre carrier of the `c_3` odd channel:\n`κ_(2,1)(q) = (q−1)³(q+1)/q²`. (Same object as `QOU.QBeta.kappaNum/kappaDen`;\npackaged here as a single field element for the factorization.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}